  "status_text": "Two small counts can stand in for a whole row of bits. Split eight bits into two groups of four and there are only 25 pairs of counts. Lean checked one circuit that reads a table of labels keyed by such counts, plus a raw word (L-lib-1425). Under a fixed limit on NOT gates, the circuit reports whether the given table can be decoded. If the table is feasible and requires a label for the word, the same circuit identifies that label. Its size bound depends on the count table and the width of the word.",
